# Releases

## Versioning

Music Cloud uses [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/) (`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`). The app is private (not an npm package); versions are for tags, GitHub Releases, and `package.json`.

| Bump | When |
|------|------|
| **MAJOR** | Deliberate shipped-product cut (`1.0.0`), or later breaking user/data changes |
| **MINOR** | New user-visible capability |
| **PATCH** | Fixes and small tweaks with no new capability |

Stay on **0.x** until a deliberate first shipped-product release (`1.0.0`). While on 0.x, bump **MINOR** for feature batches and **PATCH** for fixes.

## Branch model

- Day-to-day: feature PRs into **`dev`** (see pull-requests rule).
- Release: when a batch is ready, open a PR **`dev` → `main`**, merge, then cut the version on **`main`**.
- Tag only commits on **`main`**. Never tag from `dev`.

## Artifacts per release

1. Bump `package.json` / `package-lock.json` to `X.Y.Z` (in the release PR or on `dev` before merging).
2. Prepend a `## X.Y.Z` section to `CHANGELOG.md` (user-facing notes).
3. Merge the release PR into `main`.
4. Annotated tag on the merge commit: `git tag -a vX.Y.Z -m "vX.Y.Z"` then `git push origin vX.Y.Z`.
5. GitHub Release from that tag (`gh release create vX.Y.Z …`) using the CHANGELOG notes.
6. If the version bump landed only on `main`, merge `main` back into `dev` so versions do not diverge.

## Checklist

```text
[ ] Decide MAJOR / MINOR / PATCH from changes since last tag
[ ] Bump package.json (+ lockfile) to X.Y.Z
[ ] Write CHANGELOG.md section for X.Y.Z
[ ] Merge release PR into main
[ ] Tag vX.Y.Z on the merge commit on main
[ ] Push tag; create GitHub Release with notes
[ ] Confirm production deploy tracks main (if applicable)
[ ] Merge main back to dev if needed so versions don’t diverge
```

## Hotfixes

Branch from the release tag or from `main`, ship a **PATCH**, tag + GitHub Release, then merge back into `dev`.
